the nhl releasing its schedule for the  upcoming season this afternoon ron  futrell joining us live  with the details this is pretty exciting  news ron oh it is we're getting down to  game time almost here david  now the most interesting part of the  schedule is that teams will be playing  each other in two game mini series we'll  call it  it cuts down on the travel and just  makes everything a little safer  in this environment right now the  knights will open the season thursday  january 14th  against the anaheim ducks it'll be a  t-mold arena but no fans allowed  initially at the games we'll see what  happens  as the season goes on official workouts  don't begin until next month but the  players are all in town and gm kelly  mccrimmon  told us today that they are covered free  and  ready to get this season going the  players have been on the ice we have all  of our  players in las vegas every player is  training  so we've been able to you know i think  benefit by  players having access to ice access to  our facilities  and i expect that for our organization  at least that it's going to be  it's going to put us in a good position  going into training camp  so here's the schedule for the knights  practice begins in less than three weeks  sunday january third to be exact there's  no pre-season they'll jump straight into  that first game against anaheim  they take friday off and play anaheim  again on saturday so sort of  back-to-back with a day off in between  they're also they're going to have 56  regular season games and the final game  of the regular season for the nights  will be  saturday may 8th against the saint louis  blues now  interesting part of the schedule the  teams will all get to know each other  very well playing each other  eight times during the regular season  that could make things interesting  four teams from the west will make the  stanley cup playoffs  and those teams will play each other in  the first two rounds of the playoffs  so it'll make for an interesting nhl  season unlike any other but  i guess we we seem to be getting used to  that these days a season  unlike in the other reporting from the  newsroom ron futrell  8 sports now
 

